cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CastCheck's scores, tables or figures, please cite it. For a specific number, cite
  the permanent link of the page it came from — every score card carries a short and a long
  citation with the access date — and give the methodology version, which is published in the
  `methodology_version` column of every table and in the footer of every page.
title: "CastCheck: independent station-level verification of raw weather-model 2 m temperature forecasts"
abstract: >-
  CastCheck scores the raw 2 m temperature forecasts of operational NWP models (ECMWF IFS HRES,
  NCEP GFS) and AI models (ECMWF AIFS Single; NOAA/CIRA operational GraphCast, Pangu-Weather,
  FourCastNet v2 and Aurora from both GFS and IFS initial conditions) at 23 U.S. first-order
  stations — 22 major airports plus New York Central Park. The headline metric is the
  instantaneous 2 m temperature at 00/06/12/18 UTC
  verified against the observation at the same instants; daily extremes are published both
  like-for-like (forecast samples against observed samples) and, as a secondary comparison,
  against the NWS Daily Climate Report. No MOS, bias correction, downscaling or other
  post-processing is applied. Every station x model x lead day has a permanent URL with bootstrap
  confidence intervals and its sample size, and the full daily record is published as an open
  dataset.
